{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he established a testimony</b> — the commandments that reasoned judgment testifies to, therefore the word 'ויקם,' like 'and the house stands firm,' and 'the instruction of the commandments' (תורה המצות) whose sod is hidden from the multitudes, therefore the word 'שם,' for they received them thus from the mouth of Moses." "And the meaning of 'commanded' — as in: 'and you shall make them known to your children and your children's children' (Deuteronomy 4:9)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וקם הבית' likely alludes to a biblical idiom of establishment; rendered literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:54.899666380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}